cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use softcats, please cite the methods papers given by
  citation("softcats") in R.
title: "softcats: Regression on Predicted Categories with Calibrated Probabilities"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtkurbucz/softcats"
url: "https://mtkurbucz.github.io/softcats/"
authors:
  - family-names: Kurbucz
    given-names: Marcell T.
    email: m.kurbucz@ucl.ac.uk
    affiliation: University College London
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0121-6781"
abstract: >-
  Estimates the association between an outcome and a latent categorical
  group from calibrated class probabilities instead of predicted labels,
  with cross-fitted nuisance functions, a Neyman-orthogonal moment equation
  and robust standard errors, together with diagnostics for the conditions
  the estimate needs.
keywords:
  - R
  - predicted categories
  - class probabilities
  - calibration
  - double machine learning
